---
import CommunityLayout from '../components/CommunityLayout.astro';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="Terms of use | iDuckCalculator"
  description="The terms for using iDuckCalculator: results are estimates, not financial, tax, legal or medical advice, and the service is provided as it is."
  before="Terms of"
  mark="use"
  intro="Plain-words rules for using iDuckCalculator, provided by Basic App Company."
>
  <section class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Estimates, not advice</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">The calculators give estimates for information only. They are not financial, investment, tax, legal or medical advice. Real loans, investments, taxes and health situations depend on details a calculator cannot know, such as fees, rounding, rule changes and your own circumstances. Check important figures with your lender, a qualified adviser, the official source or a doctor before you act on them.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Rules and rates change</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">Tax, scheme and interest rules change often. Where a page depends on official rules it shows the financial year and the date those rules were read. If that date is old, check the official source yourself.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Provided as it is</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">iDuckCalculator is provided free and as it is, without a promise that it is always available or free of errors. To the extent the law allows, Basic App Company is not liable for losses that come from using the results.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Using the site</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">You may use the calculators for any lawful purpose, personal or work. Please do not copy the site wholesale, overload it with automated requests or try to break it. We may change or remove a calculator at any time.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">See the <a class="link" href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for how data is handled, or <a class="link" href="/feedback/">send feedback</a>.</p>
  </section>
</CommunityLayout>
